I audited the in-flight redesign (the 10 changed/new files) since no specific file was named. `npm run build` passes; `npm run lint` fails with **66 problems (63 errors)**. The build passing is misleading — the UI is broken in ways the compiler can't see.

## The blocker: site-wide CSS was deleted

[index.css](frontend/src/index.css) is now 7 lines — `@import "tailwindcss"` plus a dark `body` rule. The previous file defined all theme tokens (`--bg-main`, `--bg-card`, `--text-main`, `--text-dim`, `--accent`, `--accent-glow`, `--border-color`, `--nav-bg`, `--terminal-bg`, `--canvas-bg`) for both `body.light` and `body.dark`, plus the base `a` reset, print styles, and the `::view-transition-*` rules.

**502 `var(--…)` usages across 20 files** still depend on those tokens — every page except `Home.jsx`: `About`, `Skills`, `Projects`, `Experience`, `Services`, `Payment`, `Contact`, `Admin`, `ClientPortal`, `Resume`, `Reviews`, legal pages, `Footer`, `Chatbot`, `Education`.

I confirmed against the production build: there is no `--bg-main:` or `--text-main:` definition anywhere in `dist/assets/*.css`. So all those declarations are invalid and silently dropped — backgrounds go transparent (showing `App.jsx`'s slate-950 shell), borders and accent colors vanish, and text falls back to inherited white. `App.css` still has a `:root` block but it's the Vite starter file with different token names and **is imported nowhere**.

This is the single reason the site looks half-finished. Nothing else matters until it's fixed.

## Dark mode doesn't actually work

- [tailwind.config.js:3](frontend/tailwind.config.js#L3) sets `darkMode: 'class'`, but Tailwind v4 does not auto-load `tailwind.config.js` — there's no `@config` directive in the CSS. The file is dead.
- Proof from the compiled CSS: the `dark:` utilities are emitted under `@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark)`, not `.dark`. So [ThemeContext.jsx:22-30](frontend/src/context/ThemeContext.jsx#L22-L30) toggling `html.dark` changes nothing for Tailwind.
- Concrete symptom: on an OS in light mode, clicking the sun/moon button flips the emoji but the page stays light; on a dark OS, "light mode" stays dark. `Home` is the only page that reacts at all, and it reacts to the OS, not to the app theme.

## Theme ownership is split three ways

- [ThemeContext.jsx](frontend/src/context/ThemeContext.jsx) writes `html.dark` / `html.light`.
- [Navbar.jsx:44-52](frontend/src/components/Navbar.jsx#L44-L52) writes classes to **both** `html` and `body`, then calls the context toggle.
- The deleted CSS keyed its variables on `body.dark` / `body.light`, which the context never sets. So even after restoring the CSS, first paint would be unstyled unless the Navbar toggle had been clicked.
- [Navbar.jsx:40](frontend/src/components/Navbar.jsx#L40) derives `isCurrentlyDark` from `document.body.classList` — state read from the DOM instead of React; it's stale by definition.

Also: the class is applied in a `useEffect`, i.e. after paint, while `index.html` hardcodes nothing and `body` is forced dark. Expect a flash of the wrong theme on every load.

## App shell fights the pages

[App.jsx:85](frontend/src/App.jsx#L85) hardcodes `bg-slate-950 text-white` on the layout wrapper. That makes light mode structurally impossible: `Home` paints its own `#eef2f6` light surface on top of a permanent dark shell, and every not-yet-migrated page shows the dark shell through transparent backgrounds. The shell needs to be theme-driven (`bg-[var(--bg-main)]` once tokens exist) or neutral.

## Terminal boot

Good idea, three problems:

1. **Test mode shipped.** [App.jsx:56-65](frontend/src/App.jsx#L56-L65) has the `sessionStorage` guard commented out with a "uncomment before production" note. It's currently uncommented-out-of-existence: the sequence replays on every refresh, and it's ~5.3s of typing + 1.6s of pauses + 1.2s hold ≈ **8 seconds** before any content appears.
2. **The exit animation targets nothing.** [TerminalBoot.jsx:84-89](frontend/src/components/TerminalBoot.jsx#L84-L89) shrinks toward `-45vw/-45vh` assuming it lands on the navbar logo — but [App.jsx:82](frontend/src/App.jsx#L82) only renders `<Navbar />` *after* boot finishes, so it shrinks into empty space. The headline effect doesn't read.
3. **No escape hatch.** No skip button, no `prefers-reduced-motion` handling, no `role`/`aria-live`, and [line 40](frontend/src/components/TerminalBoot.jsx#L40)'s `setTimeout(onComplete, 1200)` is never cleared on unmount. The `hasStarted` ref guard also means the effect can't restart cleanly.

Compounding this: [Footer.jsx:29-50](frontend/src/components/Footer.jsx#L29-L50) uses plain `<a href="/…">` instead of `<Link>`. Every footer navigation triggers a full page reload — which replays the 8-second boot. That's a brutal combination.

## Home page

- **67 hardcoded production URLs.** `https://portfolio-px1j.onrender.com` appears 67 times across the app, e.g. [Home.jsx:59,79,87](frontend/src/pages/Home.jsx#L59). No `VITE_API_URL`, no single client module. Also no loading or error UI — if the Render instance is cold (30–60s), the page silently shows fallback copy and "No pinned projects yet."
- **Dead CMS field.** [Home.jsx:65](frontend/src/pages/Home.jsx#L65) reads `data.homeData.roles`, but the backend `contentSchema` only declares `heroTitle` and `heroSubtitle` ([server.js:142](backend/server.js#L142)). Roles can never come from the CMS, and the admin UI has no editor for them either.
- **Fields that don't exist.** [Home.jsx:324](frontend/src/pages/Home.jsx#L324) checks `repo.liveLink || repo.homepage`, but `pinnedProjectSchema` has neither ([server.js:200-209](backend/server.js#L200-L209)). The 🚀 button is decorative, never a live link.
- **Crash risk.** [Home.jsx:346](frontend/src/pages/Home.jsx#L346) calls `repo.name.replace(…)` unguarded; `name` is optional in the schema. A pin without a name white-screens the homepage (there's no error boundary).
- **Timer leak.** [Home.jsx:44](frontend/src/pages/Home.jsx#L44) nests a 2s `setTimeout` that the effect cleanup never clears.
- Typewriter indexes `roles[currentRoleIndex]` without clamping, so a shorter roles array from the CMS would throw on `undefined.substring`.

## Navigation and routes

- [Navbar.jsx:76-83](frontend/src/components/Navbar.jsx#L76-L83) dropped **Services** and **Payment** from the nav. Payment survives in the footer; **`/services` now has zero inbound links anywhere** — it's an orphaned page.
- No catch-all route in [App.jsx](frontend/src/App.jsx#L24-L49): an unknown URL renders navbar + footer around a blank body.
- `Preloader.jsx` is now unused dead code; `lucide-react` is a dependency with **zero imports**; `App.jsx` keeps an empty `useEffect` whose entire body is a comment.

## Lint, bundle, a11y

- `npm run lint` → **63 errors, 3 warnings**. Six are in files you just touched: unused `React` imports in `App`, `Navbar`, `Home`, `TerminalBoot`; `setState` in an effect in `Navbar:25`; fast-refresh violation in `ThemeContext:3`; missing `bootSequence` dep in `TerminalBoot:44`.
- One JS chunk is **1.46 MB (399 KB gzip)** with no code splitting. `three` + `drei` + `fiber` are imported eagerly by `About`, `Contact` and `Admin`, so the 3D stack loads on the homepage.
- No `aria-label` on the theme toggle or mobile menu, no `aria-expanded`, no `aria-current` on nav links. The boot overlay is a full-screen `div` with no live region.
- [index.html](frontend/index.html#L7) still has `<title>frontend</title>`, no meta description, no OG tags, and no Inter/Fira Code font despite both being referenced.

## What I'd do next, in this order

**Step 1 — stop the bleeding (highest ROI, ~1–2 hours).** Restore the token definitions from `git show HEAD:frontend/src/index.css` into the new `index.css` *underneath* `@import "tailwindcss"` — both `:root`/`.light` and `.dark` sets, the `::view-transition` rules, the `a` reset, and the print block. That one change unbreaks 20 files at once and is the difference between "redesign in progress" and "site is broken."

**Step 2 — make dark mode real (~1 hour).** Add `@custom-variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *));` to `index.css`, delete `tailwind.config.js` (v4 doesn't need it for anything you're using), and verify by toggling with the OS in the opposite mode. Then consolidate theme ownership: `ThemeContext` is the only writer of `html.light`/`html.dark`; `Navbar` calls `toggleTheme()` and derives its icon from `theme`, never from `document.body`.

**Step 3 — make the shell theme-aware (~30 min).** Replace `bg-slate-950 text-white` in `App.jsx` with token-based colors so light mode has somewhere to live. Also add an inline pre-paint script in `index.html` to set the class from `localStorage` (kills the flash), and restore the `::view-transition` rules so the circular reveal actually renders instead of a default cross-fade.

**Step 4 — de-risk the boot (~45 min).** Re-enable the `sessionStorage` guard, add a "Skip" control, honor `prefers-reduced-motion`, clear timers on unmount, render the logo during boot (or aim the shrink at the actual top-left corner), and convert footer anchors to `<Link>`.

**Step 5 — one API layer (~1–2 hours).** Add `VITE_API_URL`, a small `api.js` client, and loading/error states on `Home`. Fix the `repo.name` guard, remove the dead `roles`/`liveLink` code or add them to the backend schema, and add a route error boundary.

**Step 6 — then continue the Tailwind migration page by page** (Home → About → Skills → …), deleting the compatibility tokens only when the last page is migrated. Do not attempt a big-bang migration of the remaining 20 files in one pass; that's what produced this state.

Two things I would *not* do yet: chase the 63 lint errors repo-wide (they're pre-existing and cosmetic except the two genuine hook-rule hits), and add polish like SEO/a11y until Steps 1–3 are done — they'll be redone anyway once the theme system settles.

The fastest path to a site that looks intentional again is Steps 1–3. I can implement those now if you want.
