The interface no longer uses the “AI portfolio” template look. I replaced the whole visual language rather than adjusting colors.

**The old giveaways, all removed:** dark slate glass, emerald accents, claymorphism cards, RGB cycling buttons, gradient glows, floating pill navigation, emoji icons, the fake terminal boot, and the rotating typewriter.

**The new direction — “engineering notebook”:** warm paper, ink, one vermilion accent, Instrument Serif display type, IBM Plex Sans text, IBM Plex Mono labels, hairline rules, square corners, numbered sections, no shadows or gradients.

## What changed

- [index.css](frontend/src/index.css) — new palette (`#f3eee3` paper / `#17140f` ink / `#c93d1b` signal), warm charcoal dark mode, new `.font-display` / `.font-mono-ui` / `.eyebrow` type classes. Legacy variables are aliased to the new palette so un-migrated pages stop looking like a different site.
- [Home.jsx](frontend/src/pages/Home.jsx) — rebuilt as an editorial page: masthead with meta strip and oversized name, captioned portrait (`Fig. 01`), a `Currently` strip, a numbered project index with hairlines instead of cards, a drop-cap about note, and a large contact statement. The typewriter is gone.
- [Navbar.jsx](frontend/src/components/Navbar.jsx) — fixed paper header with `01 Work / 02 About / 03 Skills / 04 Experience`, a boxed Contact link, a `[Dark]` / `[Light]` text toggle, and a full-width mobile sheet. No glass, no pill, no emoji.
- [Footer.jsx](frontend/src/components/Footer.jsx) — a three-column colophon with index/elsewhere links and a typeset credit line.
- [Chatbot.jsx](frontend/src/components/Chatbot.jsx) — squared paper panel with mono labels, no robot emoji, no glow, no floating circle.
- [App.jsx](frontend/src/App.jsx) — terminal boot deleted entirely; the page renders immediately. Heavy pages stay lazy-loaded.
- [index.html](frontend/index.html) — Instrument Serif + IBM Plex fonts, matching theme colors.
- Interior pages (`About`, `Skills`, `Projects`, `Contact`, `Admin`, etc.) — their hardcoded cyan/neon glows were routed through the theme-aware signal color, so they inherit the new palette instead of clashing.

The redesign is live in the Preview panel at `http://localhost:5173`.

## Verification

- `npm run build` passes; initial JS is 454 kB (135 kB gzip).
- ESLint on every redesigned file: **0 problems**.
- Browser check: page renders with no console errors; the theme toggle switches light `#f3eee3` ↔ dark `#141210`, and the heading resolves to Instrument Serif.
- [PROJECT_PLAN.md](PROJECT_PLAN.md) is updated with the design direction, decisions, and verified results.

## Two honest limitations

The interior pages now share the paper/ink/vermilion palette and type, but their layouts are still the old card-based ones — fully restyling them is the next pass. Also, the CMS bio currently reads “**Iam** an 18-year-old…”, which shows up in the new drop-cap paragraph; that should be corrected in the admin editor rather than patched in code.
